    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d144-a1">

                <pb facs="0344" n="324" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg324"/>

                <head>Mr. Welles to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Navy Department,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-09-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 29, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Referring to your letter of the 2d ultimo
                    relative to the case of Edward P. Rich, I have the honor to transmit herewith,
                    in reply, a copy of a communication, dated the 21st instant, from Acting
                    Rear-Admiral T. Bailey.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GIDEON WELLES, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the
                        Navy.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
